codex
One extra robustness detail surfaced: skipping only the final division still lets boolean or other non-floating buffers enter accumulation, where `+=` can itself fail. I’m moving the generic guard ahead of accumulation as well, while keeping the final guard explicit so unchanged global values are guaranteed.
